  "note": "All 29 gameplay buildings were inspected together in the actual candidate WebGL gallery from isometric, front and back. Brick facades, pale vertical stone trims and green copper crowns create a coherent New York Art Deco family, clearly distinct from the other four regions. Upgrade silhouettes and large-lot civic/commercial structures remain readable. At 430x932 the actual game showed ordinary prebuilt houses, public buildings and regional peripheral buildings in local and overview views. Entry fee, coin toss, player roll to a prebuilt house, purchase choice, level-three close-up, rotation and return to the same purchase choice were exercised. The close-up visibly uses the approved villa model with its balcony, parapet and window details. Confirm actions are right aligned; no clipped controls were seen. Console inspection captured no errors or warnings. Attempting the header exit while the purchase overlay was open left the purchase panel unchanged; cancelling exit from an unobstructed player turn was separately validated in Harbor. This is browser visual/layout QA, not physical-phone FPS or memory profiling, and not exact reference-pixel reconstruction.",
